course: dictionary
lesson: 16091
title: Wasteful and using less
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wasteful is an adjective. It describes something that uses more of a thing than is needed, or uses it carelessly so that some is lost or thrown away. Waste means something thrown away or used for nothing, and -ful means full of, so wasteful means full of waste.
explain: «It is wasteful to leave the lights on in an empty room.» Nobody is in the room, so the light is used for nothing. The clues are «empty» and «leave the lights on», so wasteful means using energy for no good reason.
explain: Wasteful often goes with «of» or describes a habit or an object: «He was wasteful of water when he left the tap running.» «A wasteful habit» is something you do again and again without thinking, such as throwing away food that could still be eaten.
explain: Science and geography lessons teach us how to be less wasteful. Reduce, reuse and recycle help save energy, water and food, and they help look after our planet.
fact: Wasteful is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like «a wasteful habit».
fact: «Wasteful» means using more than is needed, or using something carelessly so that some is lost.
fact: Leaving lights on in an empty room, running taps and throwing away good food are all wasteful.
fact: Reduce, reuse and recycle help us be less wasteful.
fact: Wasteful is often used with «of»: «wasteful of water» or «wasteful of energy».
exercise: «Leaving the tap running while you brush your teeth is wasteful.» What does wasteful mean here? | Quick and easy | Slow and gentle | *Using more water than is needed | Cold and clean
exercise: Which one is a wasteful habit? | Walking to school | Turning off the lights when you leave a room | *Leaving the lights on in an empty room | Refilling a water bottle
exercise: «Wasteful packaging covers a small toy in far too much plastic.» What does wasteful packaging mean? | Packaging that is easy to open | *Packaging that uses more material than is needed | Packaging that is bright and colourful | Packaging made from recycled paper
test: Reduce, reuse and recycle help us be less ___. | tidy | noisy | *wasteful
test: «Throwing away good food is wasteful.» Which word tells you that food is being lost? | Food is | Good | *Throwing | Wasteful, the word itself
exam: Which word means the opposite of wasteful? | Generous | *Thrifty | Hungry | Wasteful
